			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T08:24:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement registry-backed vscode.tests namespace shim\n\nReplace the stock inline no-op stub for `vscode.tests` in EnsureVscodeAPI.ts with a dynamically-imported, registry-backed `TestsNamespace` factory in Source/Services/Handler/VscodeAPI/Tests/Namespace.ts. The previous stub's empty `TestItemCollection` silently dropped every `controller.items.add(item)` call, causing extensions like vitest, mocha-explorer, and rust-analyzer to always get `undefined` back from `controller.items.get(id)` — breaking their internal state machines.\n\nEach TestController now owns a `Map`-backed `TestItemCollection` with working add/delete/get/replace/forEach, a profile registry for `createRunProfile`, and a `TestRun` state machine tracking the full queued/started/skipped/failed/errored/passed lifecycle. `TestRun.end()` emits `tests.didChangeTestResults` on the Emitter channel with per-item results and accumulated output.\n\nRegistration is idempotent — re-registering a controller with the same id returns the existing instance, softening VS Code's duplicate-id throw to handle dev-reload double-calls. Sky-side Testing panel rendering remains gated, but all extensions importing `vscode.tests` now maintain correct internal state without crashes or silent data loss.",
			"SHA": "9b3109db2cf33aad3cff478e053cbdf444955dbd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T08:11:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance Element submodules — diff information, view column, and terminal state event bridge\n\nAdvance Cocoon, Mountain, and Sky submodules to complete the Mountain-to-Cocoon notification relay for three extension API surfaces plus extension activation routing and auth session subscriptions.\n\nSky adds three snapshot-style bridge subscriptions in the workbench integration layer: diff editor `onDidUpdateDiff` line-changes relayed as `sky:editor:diffInformationChanged`, per-group `onDidMoveEditor` tab moves relayed as `sky:editor:viewColumnChanged`, and OSC 633 B (command-input-begins) terminal interaction detection relayed via `localPty:setInteracted`. All three are guarded with try/catch so render failures never disrupt the UI pipeline.\n\nMountain fans three new IPC notifications through WindServiceHandlers: `$acceptTextEditorDiffInformationChanged`, `$acceptTextEditorViewColumnChanged`, and `$acceptTerminalStateChanged`. Also introduces `TierCommandEventBroadcast` (default Off) — when enabled, Mountain dual-emits `$acceptCommandExecuted` over Vine after gRPC `Command.Execute` from Cocoon, ensuring `onDidExecuteCommand` fires for non-locally-registered extension host commands.\n\nCocoon registers four Notification/Handler.ts cases: `$activateByEvent` defers to `ExtensionHostHandler.HandleActivateByEvent` via `setImmediate` so extension activation actually runs instead of hitting the unknown-notification fallback; `$acceptTextEditorDiffInformationChanged` emits `didChangeTextEditorDiffInformation` with a minimal TextEditor stub keyed on `modifiedUri`; `$acceptTextEditorViewColumnChanged` fires `didChangeTextEditorViewColumn` with URI and viewColumn matching VS Code's event shape; `$acceptTerminalStateChanged` updates the cached terminal's `isInteractedWith` flag and emits `didChangeTerminalState`. Additionally, the Auth namespace subscribes to each `AuthenticationProvider.onDidChangeSessions` on registration, fanning `{ added, removed, changed }` to the `auth.didChangeSessions` Emitter channel with proper disposal on provider unregister to prevent listener leaks.\n\nExtensions consuming `onDidChangeTextEditorDiffInformation`, `onDidChangeTextEditorViewColumn`, `onDidChangeTerminalState`, `onDidChangeActiveEditor`, and authentication session change events via `MakeEventSubscriber` now receive live workbench signals through the complete Mountain→Cocoon bridge.",
			"SHA": "0de337107b70105ea7304cd80362fdffcac734a8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
