				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance Element submodules — terminal shell execution event relay\n\nComplete the end-to-end bridge for VS Code terminal shell execution lifecycle events by advancing Cocoon, Mountain, and Sky submodules.\n\nSky parses OSC 633 sequences beyond the existing cwd handler — adding OscEndPattern (;D[;<exitCode>]) and OscCmdLinePattern (;E;<commandLine>) regex parsers plus a per-terminal InflightExecution Map. On OSC 633 ; C (output begins), Sky fires `localPty:shellExecutionStart` via Mountain IPC; on ; D (command finished), it fires `localPty:shellExecutionEnd` with exitCode, clearing the cached commandLine for the next execution.\n\nMountain adds two WindServiceHandlers for `localPty:shellExecutionStart` and `localPty:shellExecutionEnd`, fanning the former as `$acceptTerminalShellExecutionStart` to Cocoon and the latter as two Vine notifications: `$acceptTerminalShellExecutionEnd` and a derived `$acceptExecutedTerminalCommand` so extension subscribers observe executed commands without an additional Sky-side detection pass.\n\nCocoon registers three Notification/Handler.ts cases — `$acceptTerminalShellExecutionStart`, `$acceptTerminalShellExecutionEnd`, and `$acceptExecutedTerminalCommand` — each resolving the matching terminal from the `__terminals` context cache and assembling the VS Code event shape with the required terminal, shellIntegration, and execution sub-objects including the `{ value, isTrusted }` commandLine contract.\n\nExtension subscribers hooked via `window.didStartTerminalShellExecution`, `window.didEndTerminalShellExecution`, and `window.didExecuteTerminalCommand` now receive live notifications from OSC 633 sequence parsing in the Sky terminal layer.",
			"SHA": "d43cffe192cbca49b8b0e6aec62bc3923437449d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T22:09:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodules — bridged editor state, diagnostics, theme, and breakpoint event pipeline\n\nAdvance Cocoon, Mountain, and Sky submodules to complete the Mountain-to-Cocoon notification relay for six extension API surfaces that were previously renderer-only.\n\nCocoon adds Notification/Handler.ts cases for `$acceptDiagnosticsChanged`, `$acceptVisibleEditorsChanged`, `$acceptTabsChanged`, `$acceptVisibleRangesChanged`, `$acceptTextEditorOptionsChanged`, and `$acceptActiveColorTheme` — each pumping the Mountain notification through the matching Emitter channel consumed by extension subscribers. The `$acceptTabsChanged` handler caches tab-group snapshots on `__tabGroups` so synchronous `window.tabGroups.all` getters reflect current state.\n\nMountain fans five notification types back to Cocoon: `$acceptActiveColorTheme` in ThemesSet.rs on theme switch, `$acceptVisibleEditorsChanged`/`$acceptTabsChanged`/`$acceptVisibleRangesChanged`/`$acceptTextEditorOptionsChanged` in WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs forwarding Sky payloads, `$acceptDiagnosticsChanged` in Diagnostics.rs after Set/Clear calls, and `$onDidChangeBreakpoints` in DebugLifecycle.rs for breakpoint mutations.\n\nSky bridges four Monaco/workbench event streams through the IPC layer: `onDidScrollChange` (debounced to ~16 fps) emits visible ranges, `onDidChangeConfiguration` emits options changes, `onDidVisibleEditorsChange` emits the URI list of visible editors, and `onDidChangeActiveGroup`/`onDidAddGroup`/`onDidRemoveGroup` emit tab-group snapshots. All IPC calls are wrapped in try/catch so render failures never interrupt the UI pipeline.\n\nVS Code API subscribers inside Cocoon — `languages.onDidChangeDiagnostics`, `window.onDidChangeVisibleTextEditors`, `window.tabGroups.onDidChangeTabs`, `window.onDidChangeTextEditorVisibleRanges`, `window.onDidChangeTextEditorOptions`, `window.onDidChangeActiveColorTheme`, and `debug.onDidChangeBreakpoints` — now fire correctly for all extensions.",
			"SHA": "c378308300e06748e4f3c0b7662a01626242c877"
		}
	],
